---
export const prerender = true;
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import LegalStatus from '../components/LegalStatus.astro';
---

<Content
  kicker="Legal"
  title="Payouts & Withdrawals"
  description="How to withdraw unused avaTOK tokens, including UPI payouts in India, international payouts, verification, fees, and tax."
  image="/og/payouts.png"
  lead="How unused tokens are withdrawn, who handles the payment, and what is deducted along the way."
  updated="2026-08-05"
>
  <p>
    This page explains how withdrawals work on avaTOK. It sits alongside our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, <a href="/tokens">Tokens &amp; Wallet</a> policy,
    <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a> policy, and
    <a href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a> page.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>Unused tokens can be withdrawn.</strong> They convert back at the same fixed rate they
      were bought at — <strong>1 token = 1 US cent (US$0.01)</strong>, so 100 tokens are US$1.00.
      What reaches your account is that amount less the transfer fee, any tax (including Indian GST
      where it is due), and any charge your own bank applies. Every figure is shown before you
      confirm.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="status">1. Who pays you</h2>
  <LegalStatus variant="full" />
  <p>
    Payouts are made by the avaTOK founding team from India, under Indian law. There is no separate
    overseas entity: everything on avaTOK is operated by the same unregistered Indian business until
    we complete company registration.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>Payouts are in test and are not open to the public.</strong> Our application for a
      payment gateway as an unregistered business is under review. Until it is approved, withdrawals
      are limited to invited users, are processed manually, and may be delayed or paused. Do not
      treat avaTOK as a source of income during this period.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>2. Who can withdraw</h2>
  <p>
    Withdrawal is available to account holders with an <strong>unused token balance</strong>, where
    the account is in good standing and the withdrawal is permitted in your country. Tokens already
    spent cannot be withdrawn. Withdrawal may be unavailable while an account is suspended or under
    review, or where a payment dispute is open.
  </p>
  <p>
    The value of the balance you are withdrawing is worked out at the fixed rate of
    <strong>1 token = US$0.01</strong>. Tokens are not converted at a different rate on the way out
    than on the way in.
  </p>

  <h2>3. India — payouts to UPI</h2>
  <p>
    For customers in India, payouts are made in INR to a <strong>verified UPI address linked to your
    Indian bank account</strong>. The UPI address and the bank account behind it must belong to the
    account holder. We may decline a payout to a third party's account.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because a token is denominated at US$0.01, the USD value of the balance you withdraw is
    converted into INR using the exchange rate shown to you at the time of withdrawal.
  </p>
  <p>
    Please make sure the UPI address you enter is correct. A payout sent to a valid but incorrect
    address that you supplied may not be recoverable.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Payouts outside India</h2>
  <p>
    While we are testing, payouts are available in India only. We are not able to pay out to
    accounts outside India during this period. When that changes we will update this page.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Verification before payout</h2>
  <p>
    A withdrawal may be subject to verification of your identity and of the receiving account before
    it is released. We may ask you to confirm ownership of the bank account, UPI address, or payout
    method, and we may hold or decline a payout until any check we consider necessary is complete.
    Information collected for this purpose is handled under our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Transfer fee and GST</h2>
  <p>
    Withdrawals are subject to a <strong>transfer fee</strong>. Where GST applies in India, it is
    charged in addition. The fee and any tax are shown to you at the time of withdrawal, before you
    confirm — please read that screen, as it is the authoritative figure for your withdrawal. We do
    not publish a fixed rate here because fees can vary by method, currency, and country.
  </p>
  <p>
    The amount that reaches your account is the amount withdrawn less the fee, any tax, and any
    charge applied by your own bank or payment provider.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Tax withholding</h2>
  <p>
    Where Indian tax law requires withholding on marketplace payouts — for example TDS — we may
    withhold the required amount and remit it to the authorities. Similar withholding may apply in
    other jurisdictions where the law requires it. We may ask you for tax details before releasing a
    payout, and we may decline a payout until they are provided.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for your own tax position, including declaring your earnings and paying any
    tax due on them. Nothing on this page is tax advice.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Minimum balance</h2>
  <p>
    A minimum withdrawable balance may apply. Where it does, it is shown in the withdrawal screen.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Timelines</h2>
  <p>
    Any timeframe shown to you is an <strong>estimate, not a guarantee</strong>. Payouts depend on
    verification, on our payment partners, and on your bank. Public holidays, banking cut-offs, and
    additional checks can extend the time taken.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Failed or returned payouts</h2>
  <p>
    If a payout fails or is returned — for example because the UPI address is inactive, the bank
    account is closed, or the details do not match — we will normally return the amount to your
    token balance so you can try again with corrected details. A fee already incurred on a failed
    attempt may not be recoverable. Repeated failures may require you to re-verify the receiving
    account.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Fraud, AML, and holds</h2>
  <p>
    We may delay, hold, reduce, or decline a payout where we reasonably suspect fraud, money
    laundering, sanctions exposure, abuse of the platform, or a breach of our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, or where we are required or permitted to do so by law or
    by a payment partner. We may also set off amounts you owe us — for example a chargeback, a
    reversed transaction, or a refund we have issued to a customer — against a pending payout.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here and revise
    the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Payout and billing questions: <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>. General
    enquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@avatok.ai">hello@avatok.ai</a>. See also our
    <a href="/tokens">Tokens &amp; Wallet</a> policy and
    <a href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
